                <section class="formation-reference-section scroll-reveal reveal-up">
                    <h2>Choosing the Right Business Structure</h2>
                    <p>Every business has different objectives, ownership requirements, funding plans and regulatory considerations. A private limited company may be suitable for one business, while an LLP, One Person Company, partnership, Section 8 company or another structure may be more appropriate for another. We help clients evaluate their proposed business model and understand the practical implications of different entity structures before proceeding with formation.</p>
                    <p>Depending on the nature and objectives of the business, our entity formation support covers structures such as:</p>
                    <div class="formation-entity-grid">
                        <span>Private Limited Companies</span><span>Public Companies</span><span>Limited Liability Partnerships (LLPs)</span><span>One Person Companies (OPCs)</span><span>Partnership Firms</span><span>Section 8 Companies</span><span>Producer Companies</span><span>Joint Venture Companies</span><span>Wholly Owned Subsidiaries</span><span>IFSC Companies</span><span>Other applicable business entities</span>
                    </div>
                    <p>The objective is not simply to incorporate an entity, but to establish a structure that aligns with the business’s ownership, operations, investment and short- or long-term growth plans.</p>
                </section>

