                <section class="formation-reference-section formation-two-column formation-two-column-reverse">
                    <div class="scroll-reveal reveal-left">
                        <h2>Foreign Company Registration Services in India</h2>
                        <p>Foreign businesses entering the Indian market need to carefully evaluate how they should establish their presence. Depending on the business objective, activities, ownership structure and applicable regulations, an overseas company may consider options such as an Indian subsidiary, joint venture, branch office, liaison office or project office.</p>
                        <p>Our Foreign Company Registration support helps overseas companies and international promoters understand the available structures and the applicable corporate and regulatory requirements for establishing a presence in India.</p>
                        <p>We assist with professional and regulatory aspects related to setting up:</p>
                        <div class="formation-entity-grid formation-entity-grid-compact"><span>Subsidiaries of foreign companies</span><span>Wholly owned subsidiaries</span><span>Joint venture companies</span><span>Branch offices</span><span>Liaison offices</span><span>Project offices</span><span>Other applicable foreign structures</span></div>
                        <p>The appropriate structure depends on proposed activities and applicable foreign investment and regulatory requirements. Foreign companies may also need to consider FEMA, RBI and Companies Act requirements when establishing or operating an Indian presence.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="formation-reference-image scroll-reveal reveal-right"><img src="~/images/sonagra-corporate-business-advisory.png" alt="Foreign company registration and Indian business presence advisory" /></div>
                </section>

                <section class="formation-reference-section formation-two-column">
