                    <div class="scroll-reveal reveal-right">
                        <h2>Setting Up a Subsidiary or Indian Business Presence</h2>
                        <p>For international businesses planning long-term operations in India, incorporating an Indian subsidiary can provide a structured corporate presence. Depending on the proposed ownership and business model, the subsidiary may be established as a private or public company, subject to applicable laws and foreign investment regulations.</p>
                        <p>We provide professional assistance to international businesses and promoters in understanding the incorporation process, corporate structure and regulatory considerations involved in establishing an Indian entity.</p>
                        <p>Where a foreign company is considering a branch, liaison or project office instead, the permitted activities and applicable regulatory requirements need to be evaluated carefully. A liaison office generally serves a representative or communication role and is not intended to undertake revenue-generating commercial activities in India.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

